WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.352
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.652 --> 00:00:14.508
Unit twenty-one: Workplace Communication. In this unit, you will use formal and informal language at work.

4
00:00:15.517 --> 00:00:16.425
agenda.

5
00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:20.460
agenda means a list of topics to discuss at a meeting.

6
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.956
Let's look at the first item on the agenda.

7
00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.077
Your turn. Say: agenda.

8
00:00:28.777 --> 00:00:29.696
agenda.

9
00:00:30.683 --> 00:00:31.499
minutes.

10
00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:34.964
minutes means a written record of what was said at a meeting.

11
00:00:35.264 --> 00:00:36.788
Could you take the minutes today?

12
00:00:37.488 --> 00:00:39.722
Your turn. Say: minutes.

13
00:00:42.422 --> 00:00:43.400
minutes.

14
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:45.429
feedback loop.

15
00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:49.905
feedback loop means a regular process of giving and using feedback.

16
00:00:50.205 --> 00:00:52.588
A quick feedback loop helps the team improve.

17
00:00:53.288 --> 00:00:55.743
Your turn. Say: feedback loop.

18
00:00:58.443 --> 00:00:59.641
feedback loop.

19
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:01.756
conference call.

20
00:01:02.456 --> 00:01:05.732
conference call means a phone or video call with several people.

21
00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.670
We have a conference call with the Singapore office.

22
00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:12.011
Your turn. Say: conference call.

23
00:01:14.711 --> 00:01:16.049
conference call.

24
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:17.796
memo.

25
00:01:18.496 --> 00:01:21.389
memo means a short official note sent inside a company.

26
00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:24.095
The manager sent a memo about the new policy.

27
00:01:24.795 --> 00:01:26.588
Your turn. Say: memo.

28
00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:30.185
memo.

29
00:01:31.183 --> 00:01:32.324
prioritise.

30
00:01:33.024 --> 00:01:36.300
prioritise means to decide which tasks are most important.

31
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.204
You need to prioritise your tasks this week.

32
00:01:39.904 --> 00:01:42.440
Your turn. Say: prioritise.

33
00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.187
prioritise.

34
00:01:47.183 --> 00:01:48.010
workflow.

35
00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.058
workflow means the order in which work is done.

36
00:01:51.358 --> 00:01:53.404
The new software improved our workflow.

37
00:01:54.104 --> 00:01:56.513
Your turn. Say: workflow.

38
00:01:59.213 --> 00:02:00.411
workflow.

39
00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:03.393
follow-up email.

40
00:02:04.093 --> 00:02:08.473
follow-up email means an email sent after a meeting to confirm details.

41
00:02:08.773 --> 00:02:11.144
I'll send a follow-up email this afternoon.

42
00:02:11.844 --> 00:02:14.717
Your turn. Say: follow-up email.

43
00:02:17.417 --> 00:02:19.590
follow-up email.

44
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:22.664
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:22.964 --> 00:02:26.461
Nita, could you circulate the agenda before the conference call?

46
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.727
Of course. Shall I also take the minutes?

47
00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:35.726
That would be great, thanks. Please prioritise the budget item.

48
00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:41.167
No problem. Should I send a follow-up email afterwards?

49
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:46.169
Yes, please. Just a short memo summarising the decisions.

50
00:02:47.483 --> 00:02:50.020
Sure thing! I'll get it done by five.

51
00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:54.918
Grammar focus: Formal vs informal language.

52
00:02:55.218 --> 00:02:59.029
At work, we choose formal or informal language depending on the person.

53
00:02:59.329 --> 00:03:04.396
Formal: I would be grateful if you could send the report. Informal: Can you send me the report?

54
00:03:04.696 --> 00:03:07.694
Use formal language with clients and senior managers.

55
00:03:07.994 --> 00:03:13.268
Choose formal language for clients and senior managers, and informal language for close colleagues.

56
00:03:14.283 --> 00:03:16.843
Now read and listen. Meetings That Work.

57
00:03:17.143 --> 00:03:19.746
Many employees say that meetings waste their time.

58
00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:24.327
A clear agenda, sent in advance, helps everyone prepare.

59
00:03:25.617 --> 00:03:28.986
Someone should take the minutes, so decisions are not forgotten.

60
00:03:30.283 --> 00:03:34.489
After the meeting, a short follow-up email confirms who will do what.

61
00:03:35.783 --> 00:03:38.897
A good feedback loop keeps the workflow moving smoothly.

62
00:03:40.183 --> 00:03:42.603
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:42.903 --> 00:03:44.984
A written record of a meeting is the blank.

64
00:03:45.284 --> 00:03:48.171
A, agenda. B, minutes. C, memo.

65
00:03:52.183 --> 00:03:53.893
The answer is B: minutes.

66
00:03:55.383 --> 00:03:56.651
Which is more formal?

67
00:03:56.951 --> 00:04:01.673
A, Can you help me?. B, I would be grateful if you could help me.. C, Help me, please!.

68
00:04:05.683 --> 00:04:08.542
The answer is B: I would be grateful if you could help me..

69
00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.769
'Please find attached ...' is used in blank emails.

70
00:04:13.069 --> 00:04:16.305
A, informal. B, formal. C, text.

71
00:04:20.317 --> 00:04:22.107
The answer is B: formal.

72
00:04:23.617 --> 00:04:26.650
To decide which tasks are most important is to blank.

73
00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:30.348
A, prioritise. B, workflow. C, memo.

74
00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.640
The answer is A: prioritise.

75
00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:41.113
According to the text, what confirms who will do what?

76
00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:46.228
A, the agenda. B, a follow-up email. C, a conference call.

77
00:04:50.217 --> 00:04:52.704
The answer is B: a follow-up email.

78
00:04:54.217 --> 00:04:58.332
Now it's your turn to speak. How would you politely ask your manager for a day off?

79
00:05:03.632 --> 00:05:09.149
I'd say: I would be grateful if I could take next Friday off, as I have a family event.

80
00:05:09.449 --> 00:05:10.973
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:11.983 --> 00:05:16.807
Great work today! You learned eight new words and formal vs informal language.

82
00:05:17.107 --> 00:05:20.409
Today's value is politeness. Say please and thank you.

83
00:05:20.709 --> 00:05:23.106
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

84
00:05:23.406 --> 00:05:26.442
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

